  "summary": "A Midnight Blizzard-linked espionage cluster (GTG-20006 / Storm-2945) delivers ChocoShell, a PowerShell stager, and CornFlake, a Go backdoor, after Microsoft 365 device-code phishing and click-through Internet Shortcut lures. The stager hides its window, decodes Base64, collects browser history with PowerSploit/Empire code and beacons over HTTPS to a raw IP on /t/pixel.gif with operator-chosen stage labels, exfiltrating to /t/event. The Go backdoor persists as svchost32.exe from a fake LocalAppData\\Microsoft\\svchost32 folder via an HKCU Run value and a Schedule.Service COM object, then injects into a suspended process and harvests browser and Teams data.",
